doxygen:
========
visualizes and executes a doxygen config: doxywizard doxygen.conf
The config file is doxygen.conf


compilation + execution:
========================

****************************************************************
           ******* IMPORTANT *******
Before any compilation, edit the Makefile.conf_NCOUPL file

If the Eco3M model is to be used in a coupled mode, check that in the Makefile.conf_NCOUPL file,
the activated cpp keys are the same as the ones that should be activated when Eco3M is used alone in 1DV or 3D configuration (e.g. mesocosm configuration)

By contrast, If the Eco3M model is to be used in a 0D mode, check that the activated keys correspond to the ones for  Eco3M used alone in 0D configuration
****************************************************************

--------------------------------------------------------------------
1/ FIRST COMPILATION/EXECUTION for the generation of the Eco3M model
--------------------------------------------------------------------

1/ initialisation step (implementation of a new model configuration):
 make -f Makefile.ini clean && make -f Makefile.ini
./eco3m_ini.exe


At the end of this stage, a "call.inc" file containing the mathematical
expressions for the calculation of the biogeochemical fluxes should have been created.
Several other .inc files should have been created too. In case Eco3M is coupled to another model and becone a sub-program (key ECO3M_SUB), all these files should be copied or moved in the directory where the execution of this other model will take place.

This step should be done only once but repeated each time the model configuration (namely the represented processes, variables, parameters) is modified.

----------------------------- 
2/ SECOND COMPILATION (CALC key) 
----------------------------
  2.1/ Case where the Eco3M model is not coupled with a physical model:

     2.1.1/ check that in the Makefile.conf_NCOUPL file, the right cpp_key is selected among M0D_NCOUPL or M3D_NCOUPL (mesocosm configuration)

     2.1.2/ compilation with the following command:
           make -f Makefile.calc_NCOUPL clean && make -f Makefile.calc_NCOUPL

  2.2/ Case where the Eco3M model is coupled with a physical model:

     2.2.1/ check that in the Makefile.conf_COUPL file, the cpp_key ECO3M_SUB is activated when Eco3M is not the main program of the coupled model

     2.2.2/ compilation with the following command:
           make -f Makefile.calc_COUPL clean && make -f Makefile.calc_COUPL
     
     2.2.3/ Copy or move all the .inc files generated by the first and the second compilations in the directory where the execution of the coupled model will be done 
